# Gradle
.gradle/
build/
app/build/
.kotlin/

# Android Studio / IntelliJ
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
local.properties

# Keystores - never commit *release* signing keys
*.jks
*.keystore
# EXCEPTION: debug.keystore is deliberately committed and tracked. It holds no real security
# value (standard public debug alias "androiddebugkey", password "android" — the same Android's
# own tooling uses by default) and exists solely so every build (local or CI) is signed with the
# same certificate, so app updates between versions actually work. Never apply this exception to
# a release/production keystore.
!debug.keystore

# Logs
*.log

# Asset pipeline: generated output only.
# `tools/assets/staging/` holds sprites rendered from the SVG sources. It is
# derived, it is rebuilt by `python3 -m paperscrape_assets render`, and it must
# never be confused with `app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/`, which is the
# runtime asset directory and IS tracked. Everything else under tools/assets --
# the sources, the registry, the tooling and the reports under reports/ -- is
# tracked on purpose: the reports are the evidence for the fidelity figures
# quoted in RELEASE_HISTORY.md.
tools/assets/staging/
tools/assets/**/__pycache__/

# Internal working documents — they belong to the delivery ZIP, not to this repository.
# Machine setup and session notes, the standing brief, the design reasoning, the
# release-by-release internal history, the plan of unapproved work, the open backlogs and
# the internal delivery reports. They are the working record between the maintainer and
# whoever is doing the work, and nothing in them is written for a reader of this repository.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE ADDING A NAME HERE. A line in this file only stops a path that is *not
# already tracked*. Every path below was committed long before it was listed, so the listing
# did nothing on its own: `CLAUDE.md` sat on line 44 under a comment claiming it was never
# committed while it was public on `main` at 26 806 bytes, through eight releases. What
# removed them from the repository was one `git rm -r --cached`, once. If one of them ever
# comes back into `git ls-files`, these lines will not stop `git add -A` from carrying it
# along — the check that catches that reads the index, not this file, and it is in
# `CLAUDE.md` section 10.
#
# See AI_PROJECT_RULES.md section 10.3.
CLAUDE.md
AI_PROJECT_RULES.md
DESIGN_NOTES.md
RELEASE_HISTORY.md
ROADMAP.md
BACKLOG_*.md
docs/
release-verification/
